1 — X3 Bytecode v0.1 (spec, compact)
Overview
Purpose-built: deterministic, register-first (fast), mutation-friendly op boundaries, JIT-hints, vector ops.

Encoding: 1-byte opcode, then zero-or-many operand bytes. Little-endian for immediates. Prefix lengths for variable-sized operands.

Header: 16 bytes: magic 0x58443301 ("X3\1"), version u8, flags u8, reserved u16, constant_pool_offset u32, code_offset u32.

Sections: [header][constant_pool][function_table][code][debug?][signature?]

Endianness & alignment
All immediates: little-endian.

Opcodes aligned at byte boundaries.

Multi-byte immediates can be 1/2/4/8 bytes, encoded with a 1-byte size prefix when variable.

Registers
32 general-purpose scalar registers: R0..R31 (64-bit u64 semantics and typed widths supported).

8 vector registers: V0..V7 (128-bit, 256-bit lanes for SIMD ops).

Special registers:

PC program counter (implicit)

SP stack pointer

FP frame pointer

GAS gas remaining (u128)

ERR last trap code

Memory model
Hybrid: small operand stack + linear memory region.

STACK max 1024 entries (configurable). Use for fast temporaries.

LINEAR_MEMORY contiguous byte array, page-size 64 KiB, max pages configurable (default 16 pages).

No raw pointers; loads/stores are bounds-checked and gas-metered.

Call frames
Each CALL creates a new frame with limited local memory; frame-local linear memory permitted up to frame_mem_limit.

Gas model (deterministic)
Each opcode has a fixed gas cost table (see below).

Memory ops cost: base + per-page.

Branching has fixed cost; no branch-mispredict rounding.

VM enforces GAS >= 0, out-of-gas triggers OutOfGas Trap.

Safety & determinism rules
No floating-point on-chain. Use fixed-point Q formats if needed.

Deterministic PRNG: RAND(seed) seeded from chain-block-root or explicit input; disallowed inside on-chain @atomic unless seed provided.

Syscalls deterministic; host must return identical results for same inputs.

No filesystem or network access in on-chain execution.

No JIT allowed in runtime context; JIT only in off-chain sidecar.

