Gas model rules
Gas costs are additive deterministic integers.

GAS stored as u128, decremented per opcode.

If gas < opcode cost → OutOfGas Trap → full revert for on-chain execution.

Memory alloc/mmap cost: base + page_count * page_cost.

CALL_EVM / CALL_SVM expensive (includes cost of verification), but allowed only inside ATOMIC blocks on-chain if permitted.

Bytecode verifier (pre-exec)
Validate header + version.

Validate all opcodes known.

Verify operand sizes fit code length.

Ensure no dynamic jump targets outside code.

Build CFG and prove no unbounded recursion (max-call-depth enforced).

Confirm ATOMIC_BEGIN/ATOMIC_END balanced.

Check that CALL_FOREIGN targets have driver mapping in manifest.

Check constant pool indices.

Check gas upper bound estimate (static bound) if possible.

Signable hash: canonical serialization then sha256 → used in receipts.

